==================================== INPUT ====================================
// Test: a Query-rooted `@rootFragment` may read CLIENT-extension fields, both
// scalar and linked, under `@exec_time_resolvers`.
//
// This pins the `allow_client_fields` carve-out, which until now had NO fixture
// at all. It survives only because removing it broke four real fragments in the
// `reactive_executor` www build — a slow signal nobody runs for this crate, so
// deleting the carve-out would have left every compiler fixture green.
//
// Why it is a carve-out and not a hole. The rule rejects non-identity selections
// because at exec time they are projected from the normalized response, and a
// field the response does not carry reads back as `undefined` with no error. A
// client-extension field is not projected from the response at all — it is
// produced by resolver composition — so the failure mode the rule exists to
// prevent does not apply to it.
//
// Two distinct branches are exercised here, and they behave differently:
//   - `client_flag`, a client-extension SCALAR, is accepted by name.
//   - `client_settings`, a client-extension LINKED field, is skipped WITHOUT
//     descending into it. `theme` below it is therefore never checked. That is
//     deliberate and matches the runtime, which skips `CLIENT_EXTENSION`
//     subtrees when projecting; there is nothing under there to project.
//
// The negative control is `exec_time_resolver_query_root_reads_server_field`,
// where the same Query parent reading a SERVER field is rejected. Together they
// show the carve-out keys on the field being a client extension, not on the
// parent being `Query` alone.
//- FooQuery.js
graphql`query FooQuery @exec_time_resolvers {
  me {
    id
  }
  greeting
}`

//- Query_greeting.js
/**
 * @relayField Query.greeting: RelayResolverValue
 * @rootFragment QueryGreetingFragment
 */
graphql`fragment QueryGreetingFragment on Query {
  client_flag
  client_settings {
    theme
  }
}`

//- relay.config.json
{
  "language": "flow",
  "jsModuleFormat": "haste",
  "schema": "schema.graphql",
  "schemaExtensions": ["schema-extensions"],
  "featureFlags": {
    "enable_exec_time_resolvers_directive": true
  }
}

//- schema.graphql
type Query {
  me: User
}

type User {
  id: ID!
  name: String
}

//- schema-extensions/extension.graphql
type ClientSettings {
  theme: String
}

extend type Query {
  client_flag: Boolean
  client_settings: ClientSettings
}
